          ],
          "returnType": "NormalSource",
          "description": "Normals derived from a texture's own alpha channel, computed once. The silhouette read as a height field, which gives edges that turn away from the light without anyone authoring a map. It knows nothing about the interior of a shape, so it is a floor rather than a replacement - but it is the difference between art that reacts to light and art that does not. The source must be drawable when this is called: a texture that is still loading yields a flat map rather than waiting."
        }
